## What changed from upstream

Upstream targets the M5StickC Plus (ESP32, 135x240 portrait ST7789 over SPI, physical
buttons, IMU, AXP192 power management). This fork targets the LilyGO T-Display-S3
(ESP32-S3, 320x170 landscape ST7789 over 8-bit parallel, no buttons reachable in the
3D-printed enclosure, no IMU, no PMU):

- `src/hw.h` / `src/hw.cpp` — new. A hardware abstraction shim upstream never needed,
  replacing ~50 M5StickC-specific API call sites (display init, backlight, battery ADC,
  power-off) with T-Display-S3 equivalents.
- `src/ble_bridge.cpp` — ported from Bluedroid to NimBLE-backed BLE APIs (a newer
  Arduino-ESP32 core is required on this board to fix a BLE Secure Connections pairing bug;
  that core's bundled BLE library changed the underlying stack). The **wire protocol is
  unchanged** — see REFERENCE.md, which is otherwise untouched from upstream.
- Landscape layout (320x170) replacing the original's portrait layout (135x240): pet on the
  left, stats stacked on the right.
- Button-driven UI (screen cycling, menu, approve/deny) is not reachable on this hardware.
  Screen selection follows the persona state machine automatically; the `dizzy` and `heart`
  states, originally IMU-triggered, are reachable via an additive `cmd:"persona"` BLE
  command (documented in `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, not part of upstream's REFERENCE.md).
  Everything else in the button-driven menu/settings system was removed as unreachable.
- The IMU-driven `sleep` trigger (face-down detection) is replaced by an idle-heartbeat
  timeout, since this board has no IMU.

Kept unchanged from upstream: the 7-state persona system and its rendering logic
(`buddy.cpp`, `buddy_common.h`, all 18 species in `buddies/`), `character.cpp`'s GIF
rendering path, `stats.h`'s token/level/mood tracking, and the BLE wire protocol itself
(`REFERENCE.md`).

